instruction:
You are tasked with implementing a graph data structure in PascalABC.NET. The graph should support the addition of vertices and edges, as well as the ability to perform depth-first search (DFS) and breadth-first search (BFS) traversal algorithms.

Your task is to create a class `Graph` that supports the following operations:
1. `AddVertex(integer vertex)`: Adds a vertex to the graph.
2. `AddEdge(integer from, integer to)`: Adds a directed edge from vertex `from` to vertex `to`.
3. `DFS(integer startVertex)`: Performs a depth-first search traversal starting from the given `startVertex` and prints the visited vertices.
4. `BFS(integer startVertex)`: Performs a breadth-first search traversal starting from the given `startVertex` and prints the visited vertices.

You should use an adjacency list representation for the graph.

You are given the following code snippet as a starting point:
```pascal
type
  Graph = class
  private
    adjacencyList: Dictionary<integer, List<integer>>;

    constructor Create;
    begin
      adjacencyList := new Dictionary<integer, List<integer>>();
    end;

    // AddVertex, AddEdge, DFS, BFS methods should be implemented here
  end;

begin
  var graph := new Graph();
  graph.AddVertex(1);
  graph.AddVertex(2);
  graph.AddVertex(3);
  graph.AddVertex(4);
  graph.AddEdge(1, 2);
  graph.AddEdge(1, 3);
  graph.AddEdge(2, 4);
  graph.AddEdge(3, 4);

  Writeln('Depth-First Search:');
  graph.DFS(1);

  Writeln;
  Writeln('Breadth-First Search:');
  graph.BFS(1);
end.
```

